  ],
  "description": "Boss February 1995 service notes, main board 70567645 / PWB 00786489. Both 250 kΩ audio-taper gain sections track the Gain knob. The two differential amplifiers use 2SK184-GR devices. Their output drivers are the 1996 erratum’s 2SA1049-GR, represented by 2N3906. The 2SC2458-GR buffers use 2SC2240 equivalents. The regulated 8 V rail and buffered 4 V bias are idealized. Q4 and Q5 are represented by 60 Ω engaged switch resistances. The off dry switch, footswitch and indicator are omitted. Two 100 MΩ paths reference the series 1SS133 clipping junctions.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Gain",
      "Tone",
      "Level"
    ]
  },
